    <name>
      <text>Combined and Joint Variation 3 - Nyatiti string frequency</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The nyatiti is a traditional lyre played by the Luo community. The frequency of a nyatiti string, \(f\), varies directly as the square root of the tension, \(t\), and inversely as the length, \(l\), of the string: \(f = \frac{k\sqrt{t}}{l}\).</p>
<p>(a) A string \({@pl1@}\) cm long with tension \({@pt1@}\) N has frequency \({@pf1@}\) Hz. Find the value of \(k\).</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Use your value of \(k\) to find the frequency of a string of the same length when the tension is \({@pt2@}\) N.</p>
<p>\(f = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Substitute the first string's values into \(f = \frac{k\sqrt{t}}{l}\): \({@pf1@} = \frac{k\sqrt{ {@pt1@} }}{ {@pl1@} }\).</p>
<p>Since \(\sqrt{ {@pt1@} } = {@sq1@}\), this gives \({@pf1@} = \frac{ {@sq1@}k}{ {@pl1@} }\), so \(k = \frac{ {@pf1@} \times {@pl1@} }{ {@sq1@} } = {@pk@}\).</p>
<p>Using \(f = \frac{ {@pk@}\sqrt{t}}{l}\) with \(l = {@pl1@}\) and \(t = {@pt2@}\): \(f = \frac{ {@pk@}\sqrt{ {@pt2@} }}{ {@pl1@} } = \frac{ {@pk@} \times {@sq2@} }{ {@pl1@} } = {@pf2@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
